    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 544,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70055,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 327,
        "headingId": 544,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Seminal vesicles</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-11T10:17:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 506,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 545,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70056,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 327,
        "headingId": 545,
        "headingText": "<p>Patients often present with obstructive lower urinary tract symptoms, haematospermia, fever, or abdominal pain. A mass above the prostate may be incidentally detected by digital rectal examination or by contrast-enhanced CT.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2022-10-26T10:54:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 507,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 546,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70057,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 327,
        "headingId": 546,
        "headingText": "<p>About a dozen cases of MESTs of the seminal vesicle have been reported with sufficient histopathological description {12445241; 8382998; 16771745; 17615551; 1329693; 32743484; 3030148; 18811925; 25664946; 15598315; 18995209}. The mean age at diagnosis was 54&nbsp;years (range: 39&ndash;82&nbsp;years). The average tumour size was 67&nbsp;mm (range: 5&ndash;160&nbsp;mm).</p>",
        "timestamp": "2022-10-26T10:55:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 508,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 547,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70058,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 327,
        "headingId": 547,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-11T10:17:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 509,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 548,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70059,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 327,
        "headingId": 548,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-11T10:17:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 516,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 555,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70060,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 327,
        "headingId": 555,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumour is a well-circumscribed, solid and cystic, tan to white mass centred in the seminal vesicle. It is occasionally spongiform with cyst formations.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-11T10:17:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 510,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 549,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70061,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 327,
        "headingId": 549,
        "headingText": "<p >The tumour is composed of both stromal and benign epithelial components {25664946}. Variably sized cysts are lined with columnar or cuboidal epithelial cells with occasional hobnailing, papillary infolding, or tufting. In contrast to cystadenoma of the seminal vesicle, the stromal component of MEST is more pronounced and often hypercellular. The stroma may condense around distorted glandular spaces lined by cuboidal epithelium. Rare tumours may display stromal atypia and mitotic activity and behave in a malignant manner {12445241; 8382998; 3030148}. The stromal cells stain positively for ER, PR, vimentin, desmin, SMA, h-caldesmon, and CD34. Immunostaining for inhibin, S100, and KIT (CD117) is negative. Epithelial cells are positive for CK7, and negative for CK20, PSA, and PAP {25664946}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2022-04-14T15:47:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 511,
